clearQueue: () => void;

/**
Returns a promise that resolves when all running and queued promises have settled and the queue is empty.

Reserved slots count as active, so a promise that enqueues another promise before settling does not cause `onIdle()` to resolve early.

Calling this while the limiter is already idle resolves immediately.
*/
onIdle: () => Promise<void>;

### limit.clearQueue()

Discard pending promises that are waiting to run.

This might be useful if you want to tear down the queue at the end of your program's lifecycle or discard any function calls referencing an intermediary state of your app.

Note: This does not cancel promises that are already running.

When `rejectOnClear` is enabled, pending promises are rejected with an `AbortError`.
This is recommended if you await the returned promises, for example with `Promise.all`, so pending tasks do not remain unresolved after `clearQueue()`.

### limit.onIdle()

Returns a promise that resolves when all running and queued promises have settled and both the active slots and the waiting queue are empty.

Reserved slots count as active, so a promise that enqueues another promise before settling does not cause `onIdle()` to resolve early. Calling this while the limiter is already idle resolves immediately.

```js
import pLimit from 'p-limit';

const limit = pLimit(2);

limit(() => fetchSomething('foo'));
limit(() => fetchSomething('bar'));

await limit.onIdle();
console.log('All tasks have settled');
```

