I still used `.then()` in two places (the then-handler test and the discarded-settled check). xo's rule has an eslint-disable option used elsewhere in the repo. Let me check the existing test.js usage — it uses `// eslint-disable-line promise/prefer-await-to-then`. But those are intentional `.then`. For the then-handler test, I want to avoid `.then` on the chain. I can restructure using an async wrapper. For the discarded check, use a race via async helper.

Let me fix both to avoid lint disables where possible.

For the then-handler test: the point is to enqueue from a `.then` callback. I can still trigger it via an async function that awaits `first`:
```js
const first = limit(async () => { completed.push('first'); });
(async () => {
  await first;
  await limit(async () => { await delay(20); completed.push('second'); });
})();
```
This is effectively the same microtask timing (await == then). Good.

For the discarded check:
```js
let discardedSettled = false;
(async () => { await pending; discardedSettled = true; })();
await delay(10);
t.false(discardedSettled);
```
But an unawaited async IIFE that never settles is fine. However awaiting `pending` (never resolves) keeps it pending. Good.

Let me apply these.</think>Let me remove the remaining `.then()` uses to satisfy xo.

